Sure, here is a program in Java code that generates a list of 5 adjectives to describe a given person's personality. The program uses a pre-defined database of personality traits and a natural language processing algorithm to analyze the given person's behavior patterns and generate the list of adjectives. As an example, given the name "John," the program would output a list of adjectives such as "confident," "intelligent," "determined," "charismatic," and "honest."

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Scanner;

public class PersonalityAnalysis {

    private static List<String> personalityTraits = Arrays.asList("confident", "intelligent", "determined", "charismatic", "honest");

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.println("Enter the name of the person you want to analyze: ");
        String name = scanner.nextLine();

        List<String> behaviorPatterns = new ArrayList<>();

        System.out.println("Enter 5 statements that describe the person's behavior: ");
        for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
            behaviorPatterns.add(scanner.nextLine());
        }

        List<String> adjectives = new ArrayList<>();

        for (String behaviorPattern : behaviorPatterns) {
            List<String> words = behaviorPattern.split(" ");
            for (String word : words) {
                if (personalityTraits.contains(word)) {
                    adjectives.add(word);
                }
            }
        }

        System.out.println("The following adjectives describe the person's personality: ");
        for (String adjective : adjectives) {
            System.out.print(adjective + " ");
        }
    }
}
```

