* Description: A Java program to convert Excel files to CSV files

Click "Next" and then click "Finish".
5. Create a new folder structure for your project. I recommend creating the following folders:
* src/main/java
* src/main/resources
* src/test/java
* target

You can create these folders by clicking on the " Michel keep clicked" button in the top right corner of the IntelliJ IDEA window and selecting "New | Folder" or by using the keyboard shortcut Ctrl + Shift + N (Windows/Linux) or Command + Shift + N (Mac).
6. In the "src/main/java" folder, create a new Java class called "ExcelToCsv.java". This class will contain the code for converting the Excel file to a CSV file.
7. In the "src/main/resources" folder, create a new Excel file called "input.xlsx". This file will be used as input for the conversion.
8. In the "src/test/java" folder, create a new Java class called "ExcelToCsvTest.java". This class will contain test cases for the "ExcelToCsv" class.
9. In the "target" folder, create a new folder called "csv". This folder will contain the output CSV file.
10. Open the "ExcelToCsv.java" file and add the following code:
```java
package com.example.exceltocsv;

import java.io.File;
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.FileNotFoundException;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

import org.apache.poi.hssf.usermodel.HSSFCell;
import org.apache.poi.hssf.usermodel.HSSFRow;
import org.apache.poi.hssf.usermodel.HSSFSheet;
import org.apache.poi.hssf.usermodel.HSSFWorkbook;

public class ExcelToCsv {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        File inputFile = new File("src/main/resources/input.xlsx");
        File outputFile = new File("target/csv/output.csv");

        try (FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream(inputFile)) {
            HSSFWorkbook workbook = new HSSFWorkbook(fis);
            HSSFSheet sheet = workbook.getSheetAt(0);
            List<String[]> data = new ArrayList<>();

            for (HSSFRow row : sheet) {
                HSSFCell cell = row.getCell(0);
                String value = cell.getStringCellValue();
                data.add(new String[]{value});
            }

            try (FileWriter writer = new FileWriter(outputFile)) {
                for (String[] row : data) {
                    for (String cell : row) {
                        writer.write(cell + ",");
                    }
                    writer.write("\n");
                }
            }
        } catch (FileNotFoundException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses the Apache POI library to read an Excel file and converts it to a CSV file. It assumes that the Excel file has only one sheet and that the first row contains the column headers.

