Sure, here is a simple script that you can use to draw a line in Unity that shows the nearest rigidbody:
```
using UnityEngine;

public class DrawLine : MonoBehaviour {

    public Transform target;
    public float lineThickness = 0.1f;
    public Color lineColor = Color.red;

    void LateUpdate() {

        // Get the nearest rigidbody
        Collider[] colliders = Physics.OverlapSphere(transform.position, 100.0f);
        Rigidbody nearestRigidbody = null;
        if (colliders != null && colliders.Length > 0) {
            nearestRigidbody = colliders[0].GetComponent<Rigidbody>();
        }

        // Draw the line
        Vector3 start = transform.position;
        Vector3 end = nearestRigidbody.position;
        Debug.DrawLine(start, end, lineThickness, lineColor);
    }
}
```
This script will create a line between your transform and the nearest rigidbody. You can adjust the line thickness and color to your liking.

