You can use Base64 encoding to convert your long string into a shorter string representation that is easily shareable via URL. Remember that Base64 encoding will not always make the string shorter, but it'll make it URL-safe and shareable. Here's an example of how you can do that in JavaScript:

```javascript
// Encode the string into Base64
const encodeToBase64 = (str) => {
  return encodeURIComponent(Buffer.from(str).toString('base64'));
};

// Decode the Base64 string
const decodeFromBase64 = (base64Str) => {
  return Buffer.from(decodeURIComponent(base64Str), 'base64').toString('utf8');
};

// Sample long string
const longString = "This is a very long string that you want to encode and share via URL.";

// Encode the long string
const encodedString = encodeToBase64(longString);
console.log("Encoded String:", encodedString);

// Decode the encoded string
const decodedString = decodeFromBase64(encodedString);
console.log("Decoded String:", decodedString);
```

This example uses the `encodeURIComponent` and `decodeURIComponent` functions to make sure the Base64-encoded string is URL-safe.

