With Material-UI, you can achieve a smooth scroll on click using the `Button` component from the library. Here's how you can create a scroll on click with Material-UI:

1. First, make sure you have installed Material-UI in your project:

```bash
npm install @mui/material @emotion/react @emotion/styled
```

2. Import the required components and dependencies:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import Button from '@mui/material/Button';
```

3. Use the `Button` component from Material-UI, passing your `handleClickScroll` function:

```javascript
function SmoothScrollButton() {
  const handleClickScroll = (id) => {
    const element = document.getElementById(id.split(' ').join('-'));
    if (element) {
      // Smoothly scroll to the target element
      element.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' });
    }
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <Button variant="contained" color="primary" onClick={() => handleClickScroll('target-element-id')}>
        Scroll to target
      </Button>
    </div>
  );
}

export default SmoothScrollButton;
```

Replace `'target-element-id'` with the actual ID of the element you want to scroll to.

4. Use this `SmoothScrollButton` component in your app:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import SmoothScrollButton from './SmoothScrollButton';

function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <SmoothScrollButton />
      {/* Your content here */}
      <div id="target-element-id" style={{ minHeight: '100vh' }}>
        Content to scroll to
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

This example demonstrates how to create a Material-UI button that will scroll smoothly to your desired target element when clicked.

