Sure! Here's an example MATLAB code that uses the following methods:

1. ANOVA (Analysis of Variance): This method is used to analyze the means of multiple groups. It is used to test the presence of significant differences among the means of three or more groups. It is an omnibus test and is sensitive to both the equality of the means and the equality of the variances.

2. Tukey's post-hoc test: This method is used to identify differences among the means of multiple groups. It provides a more detailed analysis of the differences by highlighting the differences between the means in each pair of groups.

3. t-Test: This method is used to compare the means of two independent groups. It is used to test the null hypothesis that the means of the two groups are equal.

Here's the MATLAB code example:

```
data = load('paradoxical_data.mat');

group = data.Group;
weight = data.Weight;
age = data.Age;

n = length(group);

% ANOVA on group variable
stats = anova1(group);

% Tukey's post-hoc test on pairwise comparisons
pairwise_stats = ttest(group);

% Calculate p-values using ANOVA
p_values = stats.p.Values;

% Calculate p-values using t-test
pairwise_p_values = pairwise_stats.p.Values;

compare_by_oneway
``` 

