Here is a MATLAB function that performs Singular Value Decomposition (SVD):

```
function [U, S, V] = svd(A)

% SVD function
%
% Performs singular value decomposition on a matrix A.
%
% Inputs:
%   A  - Input matrix.
%
% Outputs:
%   U  - Unitary matrix.
%   S  - Diagonal matrix of singular values.
%   V  - Unitary matrix.
%
% See also:
%   linalg.svd

% Check input arguments.
if ~ismatrix(A)
  error('Input must be a matrix.')
end

% Get the dimensions of A.
n = size(A, 1);
m = size(A, 2);

% Initialize U, S, and V.
U = zeros(n, n);
S = zeros(n, m);
V = zeros(m, m);

% Compute singular values.
[U, sigma] = eig(A);

% Sort singular values in descending order.
sigma = sort(sigma, 'descend');

% Reshape U and V.
U = U(:, 1:min(n, m));
V = V(:, 1:min(n, m));

% Compute S.
S = diag(sigma);

end
```

