Here is a potential Swift code that can sort the books based on their title, author, and publication year:
```
func sortBooks(books: [Book]) -> [Book] {
    let sortedBooks = books.sorted { (book1, book2) -> Bool in
        if book1.title == book2.title {
            if book1.author == book2.author {
                return book1.year < book2.year
            }
            return book1.author < book2.author
        }
        return book1.title < book2.title
    }
    return sortedBooks
}
```
This code uses the `sorted` function to sort the books array based on their title, author, and publication year. The closure inside the `sorted` function compares two books at a time and returns a boolean value indicating which book should come first in the sorted array. The function first compares the titles of the books. If the titles are the same, it compares the authors of the books. If the authors are the same, it compares the publication year of the books. The sorted array is then returned.

