It seems like you have encountered an InputMismatchException in your Java code. This exception usually occurs when you try to read an input of a different type than what's expected. For instance, if you expect an integer value but receive a string or a float.

To help you solve this issue, please make sure you are providing the correct input type. You can use hasNextInt(), hasNextDouble(), or hasNext() methods of the Scanner class to check if the input data matches the expected type before attempting to read it. Also, you can add a user-friendly prompt to let the user know the expected type of input.

Here's an example of how to handle a scenario like this:

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class RetrieveInputExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scan = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.println("Please enter an integer value:");

        while (!scan.hasNextInt()) {
            System.out.println("Invalid input. Please enter an integer value:");
            scan.next(); // Discard the invalid input and wait for a new input
