Bubble Sort is a simple algorithm that works by repeatedly swapping adjacent elements if they are in the wrong order. Here's a step-by-step guide on how to implement a Bubble Sort algorithm in C#:

1. First, create a new C# project or open an existing one.
2. In the `Main` method, add a sample array that you want to sort using Bubble Sort, like this:

```csharp
int[] sampleArray = {5, 8, 3, 1, 6};
```

3. Now, create a method called `BubbleSort` which will receive the array as a parameter:

```csharp
public static int[] BubbleSort(int[] arrayToSort)
{
    // Bubble sort implementation
}
```

4. Inside the `BubbleSort` method, implement the Bubble Sort algorithm using nested loops:

```csharp
public static int[] BubbleSort(int[] arrayToSort)
{
    int arrayLength = arrayToSort.Length;

    for (int i = 0; i < arrayLength - 1; i++)
    {
        for (int j = 0; j < arrayLength - 1 - i; j++)
        {
            if (arrayToSort[j] > arrayToSort[j + 1])
            {
                // Swap arrayToSort[j] and arrayToSort[j + 1]
                int temp = arrayToSort[j];
                arrayToSort[j] = arrayToSort[j + 1];
                arrayToSort[j + 1] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
    return arrayToSort;
}
```

5. Finally, in your `Main` method, call the `BubbleSort` method with the sample array, print the sorted array, and test the program:

```csharp
using System;

namespace BubbleSortExample
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            int[] sampleArray = {5, 8, 3, 1, 6};
            int[] sortedArray = BubbleSort(sampleArray);

            Console.WriteLine("Sorted array: ");
            foreach (int item in sortedArray)
            {
                Console.Write(item + " ");
            }
        }

        public static int[] BubbleSort(int[] arrayToSort)
        {
            int arrayLength = arrayToSort.Length;

            for (int i = 0; i < arrayLength - 1; i++)
            {
                for (int j = 0; j < arrayLength - 1 - i; j++)
                {
                    if (arrayToSort[j] > arrayToSort[j + 1])
                    {
                        // Swap arrayToSort[j] and arrayToSort[j + 1]
                        int temp = arrayToSort[j];
                        arrayToSort[j] = arrayToSort[j + 1];
                        arrayToSort[j + 1] = temp;
                    }
                }
            }
            return arrayToSort;
        }
    }
}
```

By running the program, you'll see the sorted array [1, 3, 5, 6, 8] printed in the console. Now you have successfully implemented Bubble Sort in C#! Remember that Bubble Sort isn't the most efficient sorting algorithm, and it's recommended to use other algorithms like Quick Sort or Merge Sort for larger datasets.

