In order to generate a word that is the antonym of "lonely" and has at least three syllables, you can use a Java program to find all possible permutations of the input string and then check each of them against a list of known antonyms. Alternatively, you can download a Java library for antonyms search and look for antonyms directly.

Here's a sample Java program to generate all possible permutations of the given string and check them against a list of known antonyms:

```java
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.Set;

public class AntonymGenerator {
    // Replace this list with a comprehensive list of antonyms for "lonely"
    private static final Set<String> LONELY_ANTONYMS = new HashSet<String>() {{
        add("friendly");
        add("sociable");
        add("companionable");
        // Add more antonyms here
    }};

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String input = "lonely";
        Set<String> permutations = new HashSet<>();
        permute("", input, permutations);

        for (String word : permutations) {
            if (LONELY_ANTONYMS.contains(word)) {
                System.out.println("Found antonym of 'lonely': " + word);
                break;
            }
        }
    }

    private static void permute(String prefix, String remaining, Set<String> permutations) {
        if (remaining.length() == 0) {
            permutations.add(prefix);
        } else {
            for (int i = 0; i < remaining.length(); i++) {
                char c = remaining.charAt(i);
                String newPrefix = prefix + c;
                String newRemaining = remaining.substring(0, i) + remaining.substring(i + 1);
                permute(newPrefix, newRemaining, permutations);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Note that this approach is not very efficient, as it generates all permutations even if the antonym is found early in the process. A more efficient approach could involve looking for antonyms directly, but this would require a more advanced algorithm or a third-party library.

Keep in mind that this particular example is limited to antonyms for the word "lonely" included in `LONELY_ANTONYMS`. To generate antonyms for other words, you would need to have a more comprehensive list of antonyms. This can be achieved by using a lexicon database or an NLP library that can provide antonyms directly.

