How can I modify this code to include even more detailed annotations and captions for each stage of mitosis using MATLAB?

output:
Great question!

One approach to enhancing illustrations and providing detailed annotations for each stage of mitosis in MATLAB is to incorporate annotations in the figure using text objects. Here's an example:

<pre><code>figure;
subplot(2,2,1)
imshow('prophase.png');
title('Prophase');
text(100,100,{'- Chromosomes condense and become visible',' - Spindle fibers begin to form',' - Nuclear membrane begins to break down'},'BackgroundColor',[.7 .9 .7])
annotate(gca,'Scaled'); % add annotation to indicate that all subplots have the same scale
subplot(2,2,2)
imshow('metaphase.png');
title('Metaphase');
text(100,100,{'- Chromosomes align in the center of the cell',' - Spindle fibers attach to the centromeres of each chromosome',' - Nuclear membrane fully breaks down'},'BackgroundColor',[.7 .9 .7])
annotate(gca,'Scaled'); % add annotation to indicate that all subplots have the same scale
subplot(2,2,3)
imshow('anaphase.png');
title('Anaphase');
text(100,100,{'- Spindle fibers pull the chromosomes apart',' - Chromosomes are pulled to opposite poles of the cell'},'BackgroundColor',[.7 .9 .7])
annotate(gca,'Scaled'); % add annotation to indicate that all subplots have the same scale
subplot(2,2,4)
imshow('telophase.png');
title('Telophase');
text(100,100,{'- Chromosomes reach the poles of the cell',' - Spindle fibers disintegrate',' - Nuclear membrane reforms around each set of chromosomes'},'BackgroundColor',[.7 .9 .7])
annotate(gca,'Scaled'); % add annotation to indicate that all subplots have the same scale
annotate(gca,'left','textfont','Arial','fontsize','10','x','-0.15') % add x-axis annotation
annotate(gca,'right','textfont','Arial','fontsize','10','x','0.9'); % add x-axis annotation
annotate(gca,'bottom','textfont','Arial','fontsize','10','y','-6') % add y-axis annotation
annotate(gca,'top','textfont','Arial','fontsize','10','y','0.8') % add y-axis annotation
</code></pre>

In this modified code, we add text objects at the top and bottom of each subplot to describe the stage of mitosis using the text function. We also add annotations at the bottom-left and top-right corners of each subplot to indicate the scale for the figure. You can add more annotations and captions as needed, for example, within the text objects themselves, to highlight specific details or processes that are occurring during each stage of mitosis.

