Of course! I'm here to help. Let's start by creating the HTML structure for the financial literacy program:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Financial Literacy Program</title>
    <style>
        /* Add your CSS styling here */
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Financial Literacy Program</h1>
    <p>Enter your financial information:</p>
    <form id="financialForm">
        <label for="income">Monthly Income:</label>
        <input type="number" id="income" name="income" step="0.01" required><br>

        <label for="expenses">Monthly Expenses:</label>
        <input type="number" id="expenses" name="expenses" step="0.01" required><br>

        <label for="debt">Total Debt:</label>
        <input type="number" id="debt" name="debt" step="0.01" required><br>

        <button type="submit">Submit</button>
    </form>

    <div id="results" style="display: none;">
        <h2>Recommendations</h2>
        <p id="savingsMessage"></p>
        <p id="debtMessage"></p>
    </div>

    <script>
        // Add your JavaScript code here

        document.getElementById('financialForm').addEventListener('submit', e => {
            e.preventDefault();

            const income = parseFloat(document.getElementById('income').value);
            const expenses = parseFloat(document.getElementById('expenses').value);
            const debt = parseFloat(document.getElementById('debt').value);

            const savings = (income - expenses).toFixed(2);
            document.getElementById('savingsMessage').innerText = `You can save $${savings} per month.`;

            if (debt > 0) {
                const monthsToPayOff = Math.ceil(debt / savings);
                const amountToSave = (debt / monthsToPayOff).toFixed(2);
                document.getElementById('debtMessage').innerText = `You can pay off your debt in approximately ${monthsToPayOff} months by allocating $${amountToSave} per month towards it.`;
            } else {
                document.getElementById('debtMessage').innerText = 'Congratulations, you have no debt!'
            }

            document.getElementById('results').style.display = 'block';
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code sets up an HTML page with a simple form for users to enter their monthly income, expenses, and total debt. The JavaScript code calculates the potential savings per month and provides recommendations on paying off debt.

This is just a basic structure. You can enhance it with more functionalities like adding multiple expense categories, visualizations, or any other feature you'd like to include in the financial literacy program.

