To create a Lambda function that fetches product headers and puts them onto a SQS queue, you can follow this implementation:

1. First, install the required packages for AWS SDK and Typescript.

```bash
npm install --save aws-sdk @types/aws-sdk
```

2. Create a utility file `sendSqsBatch.ts` to define a function for sending a batch of messages to the SQS queue.

```typescript
// sendSqsBatch.ts
import { SQS } from 'aws-sdk';

const sqs = new SQS();

export const sendProductsToSQS = async (queueUrl: string, products: queryResource[]) => {
  // Split products into batches of 10, since SQS supports sending a maximum of 10 messages in a single batch
  const batchSize = 10;
  const productBatches = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < products.length; i += batchSize) {
    productBatches.push(products.slice(i, i + batchSize));
  }

  const sendMessageBatchPromises = productBatches.map(async (productBatch, index) => {
    const entries = productBatch.map(product => ({
      Id: product.uuid,
      MessageBody: JSON.stringify(product)
    }));

    const params: SQS.SendMessageBatchRequest = {
      QueueUrl: queueUrl,
      Entries: entries
    };

    try {
      const response = await sqs.sendMessageBatch(params).promise();
      console.log(`Batch ${index + 1} sent successfully. Response:`, response);
      return response;
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(`Failed to send batch ${index + 1}. Error:`, error);
      throw error;
    }
  });

  return Promise.all(sendMessageBatchPromises);
};
```

3. Modify the handler function in the provided code to call the `sendProductsToSQS()` function.

```typescript
// handler.ts
