  console.log("Token received: " + token);
  // Switch to the current object thread and perform actions with the token
});
```

In this example, we use the `fetch` API to get the token. When the request is successful, the `callback` function is called with the token as the argument, allowing you to switch to the current object thread and perform actions with the token.

