First, make sure you have the .NET SDK installed. You can download it from: https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download

Once installed, follow these steps:

1. Open a terminal or command prompt, and create a new project with the following command:

```
dotnet new webapi -n AsyncRestApiService
```

2. After the project is created, navigate to the project folder:

```
cd AsyncRestApiService
```

3. Open the `Program.cs` file and replace the content with:

```csharp
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Builder;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http;
using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting;
using Newtonsoft.Json;

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// Add services to the container.
builder.Services.AddControllers();

var app = builder.Build();

// Configure the HTTP request pipeline.
if (!app.Environment.IsDevelopment()) 
{
    app.UseExceptionHandler("/Error");
    app.UseHsts();
}

app.UseHttpsRedirection();
app.UseAuthorization();
app.UseRouting();
app.MapControllers();

app.UseEndpoints(endpoints =>
{
    endpoints.MapPost("/api/posts", ReceiveAndReturnPost);
});

app.Run();

async Task ReceiveAndReturnPost(HttpContext context)
{
    var receivedPost = await JsonSerializer.DeserializeAsync<Post>(context.Request.Body);
    if (receivedPost == null)
    {
        context.Response.StatusCode = StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest;
        return;
    }

    context.Response.ContentType = "application/json";
    await JsonSerializer.SerializeAsync(context.Response.Body, receivedPost, new JsonSerializerOptions
    {
        PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase
    });
}

public class Post
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Title { get; set; }
    public string Content { get; set; }
}
```

This code sets up a simple REST API `POST` endpoint at `/api/posts`, which receives a `Post` object and returns it back to the client as JSON.

4. Run the API with:

```
dotnet run
```

By default, the API will be available at `http://localhost:5000` for HTTP and `https://localhost:7001` for HTTPS. To change the port to 8080, update the `appsettings.json` file:

```json
