What Go code can I use to extract information from an alcohol bottle label? For example, given the label "an Irish Whiskey with a smooth finish", how can I parse the text to extract the type of alcohol and its flavor profile?
Here is a sample Go code that can extract information from the label:
package main
import (
	"fmt"
	"regexp"
)
func main() {
	label := "an Irish Whiskey with a smooth finish"

	// Extract alcohol type
	typeRegex := regexp.MustCompile(`[a-zA-Z]+\s+[a-zA-Z]+`)
	alcoholType := typeRegex.FindString(label)

	// Extract flavor profile
	flavorRegex := regexp.MustCompile(`\b\w+ finish\b`)
	flavorProfile := flavorRegex.FindString(label)

	fmt.Printf("Alcohol Type: %s\n", alcoholType)
	fmt.Printf("Flavor Profile: %s\n", flavorProfile)
}

