Assuming you would like to add a click event listener to each card, you can modify the generateCard function to include a set of click event listeners for each card. Here is an example of how you can modify the function:

```
function generateCard() {
  const suits = ['spades', 'hearts', 'diamonds', 'clubs'];
  const ranks = ['ace', '2', '3', '4', '5', '6', '7', '8', '9', '10', 'jack', 'queen', 'king'];

  let cardsHTML = '';

  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
    const suitIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * suits.length);
    const rankIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * ranks.length);

    const cardSuit = suits[suitIndex];
    const cardRank = ranks[rankIndex];

    const cardImage = document.createElement('img');
    cardImage.src = 'images/'+cardRank+'_of_'+cardSuit+'.png';
    cardImage.style.margin = '5px';
    cardImage.width = '100px';
    cardImage.height = '130px';

    const cardBody = document.createElement('div');
    cardBody.appendChild(cardImage);
    cardBody.appendChild(document.createTextNode(cardRank + ' ' + cardSuit));

    const card = document.createElement('div');
    card.appendChild(cardBody);

    card.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
      const clickedCardIndex = parseInt(card.previousElementSibling.getAttribute('id'));
      console.log(clickedCardIndex);
    });

    cardsHTML += `
      <div class="row">
        <div class="card" id="${cardIndex}">
          ${cardImage.outerHTML}
        </div>
      </div>
    `;
  }

  const numbersContainer = document.getElementById('numbers-container');
  numbersContainer.innerHTML = cardsHTML;
}
```

In this modified function, we create an image element for each card using a separate image URL. We also create a body element for each card that includes the card rank and suit. We then create a parent div element that includes the card image and body.

Next, we add a click event listener to each card element that listens for a click event on the card itself. When a card is clicked, we extract the index of the card from its parent element's ID attribute, which we assume is set to a sequence of numbers identifying the card's order.

Finally, we generate a HTML string containing all the card div elements and their associated image elements, and then set the innerHTML of the numbers container to this string to display all the cards.

