What are some practical tips for novice Java programmers looking to improve their coding skills? Here are three suggestions:
1. Practice writing code every day, even if it's just for a few minutes. This will help you get into the habit of thinking like a programmer and will improve your coding skills over time.
2. Read books, articles, and tutorials on Java programming. There are many great resources available online and in print that can help you learn new concepts and improve your understanding of the language.
3. Join online communities and discussion groups for Java programmers. These can be great places to ask questions, get feedback on your code, and connect with other developers who share your interests.
As for specific Java code, here's an example of a program that calculates the factorial of a number:
import java.util.Scanner;
public class Factorial {
   public static void main(String[] args) {
      Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);
      System.out.print("Enter a number: ");
      int num = input.nextInt();
      int fact = 1;
      for (int i = 1; i <= num; i++) {
         fact = fact * i;
      }
      System.out.println("Factorial of " + num + " is " + fact);
   }
}

