To create an AWS CDK script to create an SQS queue and a Lambda function associated with it, you'll need to have the AWS CDK installed and configured on your system. You can follow the AWS CDK Getting Started guide to set it up: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/latest/guide/getting_started.html

Once you have the AWS CDK set up, you can use the following example to create a stack that contains an SQS queue and a Lambda function associated with it.

1. Create a new CDK app:

```bash
cdk init app --language typescript
```

2. Change directory to the CDK app you just created:

```bash
cd YOUR_APP_NAME
```

3. Install necessary npm packages:

```bash
npm install @aws-cdk/aws-sqs @aws-cdk/aws-lambda @aws-cdk/aws-lambda-event-sources
```

4. Replace the contents of the `lib/YOUR_APP_NAME-stack.ts` file with the following code:

```typescript
import * as cdk from '@aws-cdk/core';
import * as sqs from '@aws-cdk/aws-sqs';
import * as lambda from '@aws-cdk/aws-lambda';
import * as lambdaEventSources from '@aws-cdk/aws-lambda-event-sources';

export class MyAppStack extends cdk.Stack {
  constructor(scope: cdk.Construct, id: string, props?: cdk.StackProps) {
    super(scope, id, props);

    // Create SQS queue
    const queue = new sqs.Queue(this, 'MyQueue', {
      visibilityTimeout: cdk.Duration.seconds(30),
      fifo: true,
      queueName: 'MyFifoQueue.fifo',
    });

    // Create Lambda function
    const myLambda = new lambda.Function(this, 'MyLambda', {
      runtime: lambda.Runtime.NODEJS_14_X,
      handler: 'index.handler',
      code: lambda.Code.fromAsset('lambda'),
    });

    // Associate Lambda function to SQS queue
    myLambda.addEventSource(new lambdaEventSources.SqsEventSource(queue));
  }
}
```

Make sure to replace `YOUR_APP_NAME` with the actual name of your app.

5. Create a new folder named `lambda` at the root of your CDK app, and create a file named `index.ts` inside it. Add this code for the Lambda function:

```javascript
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  console.log('Event:', JSON.stringify(event, null, 2));

  for (const record of event.Records) {
    console.log('Message body:', record.body);
  }
};
```

6. Deploy your CDK app:

```bash
cdk deploy
```

This script will create an SQS queue named `MyFifoQueue.fifo` and a Lambda function named `MyLambda`. The Lambda function will be triggered when new messages arrive in the queue. The Lambda function handler is set to the `index.handler` exported from the `index.ts` file in the `lambda` folder. You can modify the Lambda handler code to handle messages from the queue as needed.

