Sure, here is an example of MATLAB code that can be used to create a word cloud based on the most commonly used adjectives to describe the character "Alice" in "Alice in Wonderland":

```
% Load the text of Alice in Wonderland
% This is a pre-loaded dataset in MATLAB
text = get('alice_in_wonderland.txt');

% Extract all adjectives from the text
adjectives = regexp(text, '^[a-z]+\\b(?=\\w*\\b)', 'ignorecase');

% Count the number of times each adjective appears
adjective_counts = table(adjectives);

% Sort the adjectives by descending count
sorted_adjectives = sort(adjective_counts, 'descend');

% Create a word cloud using the most commonly used adjectives
wordcloud(' ', sorted_adjectives(:, 1), 'fontSize', 24);
```

This code will create a word cloud with the most commonly used adjectives to describe the character "Alice" in "Alice in Wonderland". The adjectives will be sorted by descending count, so the most common adjective will appear at the top of the word cloud. You can then analyze the context and tone in which these adjectives are used to gain a better understanding of Alice's personality and traits.

For example, one of the most commonly used adjectives to describe Alice is "curious". This adjective is used to describe Alice's inquisitive nature and her desire to explore the world around her. Another commonly used adjective is "brave". This adjective is used to describe Alice's courage and her willingness to stand up for what she believes in. These adjectives provide insights into Alice's personality and traits that can help us to better understand her character.

