To develop a cross-platform mobile application for iOS and Android using React Native framework that fetches and displays a restaurant's menu list from a remote API endpoint, you will need to follow these steps:

1. Install the React Native CLI.
2. Create a new React Native project.
3. Install the necessary dependencies.
4. Create a component that will display the menu list.
5. Fetch the menu list from the remote API endpoint.
6. Display the menu list in the component.
7. Add items to the cart.
8. Place an order securely using payment gateway integration.
9. Allow users to view and rate restaurants based on their experiences.
10. Design the UI in a modern, elegant, and responsive way.

Once you have completed these steps, you will have a working cross-platform mobile application that can be used to order food from restaurants.

Here are some additional details on each step:

1. To install the React Native CLI, you can use the following command:

```
npm install -g react-native-cli
```

2. To create a new React Native project, you can use the following command:

```
react-native init MyApp
```

3. To install the necessary dependencies, you can use the following command:

```
npm install
```

4. To create a component that will display the menu list, you can create a file called `App.js` and add the following code:

```
import React, { Component } from 'react';
import { View, Text, StyleSheet } from 'react-native';

class App extends Component {
 state = {
  menuList: []
 };

 componentDidMount() {
  fetch('https://example.com/api/v1/menu')
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(data => {
   this.setState({
    menuList: data
   });
  });
 }

 render() {
  return (
   <View style={styles.container}>
    <Text style={styles.title}>Menu List</Text>
    <ul style={styles.list}>
     {this.state.menuList.map(item => (
      <li key={item.id}>{item.name}</li>
     ))}
    </ul>
   </View>
  );
 }
}

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
 container: {
  flex: 1,
  backgroundColor: '#fff'
 },
 title: {
  fontSize: 24,
  fontWeight: 'bold'
 },
 list: {
  margin: 8
 }
});
```

5. To fetch the menu list from the remote API endpoint, you can use the `fetch()` function. The `fetch()` function takes two arguments: the URL of the API endpoint and a callback function. The callback function will be called when the request has been completed.

6. To display the menu list in the component, you can use the `render()` method. The `render()` method takes one argument: a React element. The React element can be a simple text string, a list of elements, or an array of elements.

7. To add items to the cart, you can use the `Cart` component. The `Cart` component takes two arguments: the list of items in the cart and the total price of the cart.

8. To place an order securely using payment gateway integration, you can use a third-party payment gateway such as Stripe or PayPal.

