To display the 3 latest blog posts on a WordPress page, you can create a custom page template or use a shortcode in your existing page. I'll provide you with both methods.

**Method 1: Custom Page Template**

1. Create a new file named `three-latest-posts.php` in your theme folder (wp-content/themes/your-theme-folder/).
2. Paste the following code at the top of the file:

```php
<?php
/* Template Name: Three Latest Posts Page */
get_header(); ?>
```

3. Now, add the code that will display the 3 latest blog posts with the featured image, title, and excerpt:

```php
<div class="three-latest-posts">
    <?php
        $args = array(
            'posts_per_page' => 3,
            'post_type' => 'post',
            'post_status' => 'publish',
            'orderby' => 'date',
            'order' => 'DESC'
        );
        $latest_posts = new WP_Query($args);
         if ($latest_posts->have_posts()) :
            while ($latest_posts->have_posts()) : $latest_posts->the_post(); ?>
                <div class="latest-post">
                    <div class="post-featured-image">
                        <?php the_post_thumbnail(); ?>
                    </div>
                    <h2 class="post-title">
                        <a href="<?php the_permalink(); ?>"><?php the_title(); ?></a>
                    </h2>
                    <div class="post-excerpt">
                        <?php the_excerpt(); ?>
                    </div>
                </div>
            <?php endwhile;
            wp_reset_postdata();
         endif;
    ?>
</div>
```

4. Finally, add `get_footer();` at the end of the file to include the footer.

```php
<?php get_footer(); ?>
```

5. Save the file and go to your WordPress admin dashboard.
6. Create a new page (Pages > Add New), and in the Page Attributes section, choose the "Three Latest Posts Page" template. Publish the page and view it.

**Method 2: Shortcode**

Add the following code to your theme's `functions.php` file:

```php
function display_three_latest_posts() {
    $args = array(
        'posts_per_page' => 3,
        'post_type' => 'post',
        'post_status' => 'publish',
        'orderby' => 'date',
        'order' => 'DESC'
    );
    $latest_posts = new WP_Query($args);
    $output = '';

    if ($latest_posts->have_posts()) :
        $output .= '<div class="three-latest-posts">';
        while ($latest_posts->have_posts()) : $latest_posts->the_post();
            $output .= '<div class="latest-post">';
            $output .= '<div class="post-featured-image">' . get_the_post_thumbnail() . '</div>';
            $output .= '<h2 class="post-title"><a href="' . get_the_permalink() . '">' . get_the_title() . '</a></h2>';
            $output .= '<div class="post-excerpt">' . get_the_excerpt() . '</div>';
            $output .= '</div>';
        endwhile;
        wp_reset_postdata();
        $output .= '</div>';
    endif;

    return $output;
}
add_shortcode('three_latest_posts', 'display_three_latest_posts');
```

Now, you can use the `[three_latest_posts]` shortcode in any page or post content to display the 3 latest blog posts with the featured image, title, and excerpt.

Remember to style the output using CSS classes in your theme's `style.css` file to match your desired appearance.

