There are several methods you can use to access a JSON file stored on an AWS S3 bucket from a React Native mobile application. Here are some common methods:

1. HTTP request
You can use HTTP requests to fetch the JSON file from the S3 bucket, using the URL that points to the location of the file. Here's some sample code that shows how to do this:

```jsx
axios.get(url)
  .then(res => {
    const data = res.data;
    // Parse JSON using react-native's built-in JSON module
    const jsonData = JSON.parse(String.fromCharCode.apply(null, new Uint8Array(
          data
        )
      )
    );
    // Do something with the parsed JSON data
    console.log(jsonData);
  })
  .catch(err => console.log(err));
```

2. AWS SDK for iOS
You can use the AWS SDK for iOS to access your S3 bucket. The SDK provides a library of classes and APIs to interact with AWS services, including S3. Here's some sample code that shows how to use the SDK:

```jsx
let s3 = AWS.config.defaultCredentialProviderFromCocoaKeychainOrUI([]);
let params = {
  Bucket: "your-bucket-name",
  Key: "path/to/your/file",
};
s3.downloadFile(params).promise().then(function(result) {
  let data = result.Body.toString('utf-8');
  // Do something with the downloaded file
}).catch(function(err) {
  console.log(err, err.stack);
});
```

3. Third-party libraries
There are several third-party libraries and tools available that can help you access your S3 bucket from a React Native mobile app. We'll focus on the two most popular ones: react-native-aws and AWS Amplify.

Using react-native-aws library, you can access your S3 bucket with the following code:

```jsx
import AWS from 'aws-sdk';
const s3 = new AWS.S3();

s3.getObject({
  Bucket: 'your-bucket-name',
  Key: 'path/to/your/file'
}, (err, data) => {
  if (err) {
    console.log(err);
  } else {
    const jsonData = JSON.parse(data.Body.toString('utf-8'));
    // Do something with the parsed JSON data
  }
});
```

Using AWS Amplify library, you need to set up the service in your app and then use it to access your S3 bucket. Here's the basic setup:

1. Ensure that you have an AWS account and it is configured to use the services you will be accessing.
2. Install the AWS Amplify library using npm: `npm install @aws-amplify/core`
3. Add the following code to your App.js file:

```jsx
import Amplify from '@aws-amplify/core';

Amplify.addAuth({
  idp: 'aws',
  authenticator: 'cognitoUserPool',
  roleRelayEnabled: true,
});

await Amplify.configure(this.context, { loggerLevel: 'info' });

Amplify.REST.configure();

const s3 = Amplify.configure().Resources.AwsSingleService.path('s3');

const data = await s3.get('my-bucket', 'my-file');

const jsonData = JSON.parse(data, function(key, value) {
  if (key === '') { return undefined; }
  return value;
});
```

Note: Since the focus of this answer is to provide methods to fetch and parse JSON data from JSON files stored in AWS S3 bucket, the security aspects of accessing and storing sensitive data on the AWS S3 is left unaddressed.</s> 
