You can use the HTTPClient class from the Microsoft.AspNet.WebAPI.Client namespace to send requests to the API and receive the response. You will need to request an access token from the API by sending a login request with valid credentials. After getting the access token, you can use it to authenticate subsequent requests to the API.

Here is an example code snippet that shows how to download a file from an API protected by authentication:

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNet.WebApi;
using Microsoft.AspNet.WebApi.Client;
using System;
using System.IO;

// Create a Configuration object to store API keys
var config = new CredentialConfiguration { ApiKeyName = "your_api_key", ApiKeyValue = "your_api_key_value" };

// Create an HttpClient instance and set the necessary properties
HttpClient client = new HttpClient(new CredentialConfiguration(config));
client.BaseAddress = new Uri("https://api.example.com");

// Authenticate the request by sending a login request with valid credentials
HttpResponseMessage loginResponse = client.SendAsync("api/authenticate").Result;
int statusCode = loginResponse.StatusCode;
string cookies = loginResponse.Headers.GetValues("Set-Cookie")[0];

// Use the access token and cookies to authenticate subsequent requests
